 "article": {
  "title": "The Rise of the Weekend Marathon",
  "topic": "体育（大众跑步·全民健身）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 314,
  "paras": [
   "In the past, a marathon was a race for a few elite athletes. Today, on almost any weekend, thousands of ordinary people line up at the start of a forty-two kilometre course. The change did not happen by chance. As incomes rose and health became a personal goal, running turned into a hobby that almost anyone can begin with a pair of shoes.",
   "The appeal is simple. Running requires little equipment and fits easily into a busy day. Doctors point out that regular exercise is an effective way to control weight, strengthen the heart and lower the risk of many illnesses. Many runners also say the hours spent on the road give them something money cannot buy: a clear mind and a sense of calm. For them, the weekly run is less a competition than a way to reset the mind after a long week of work.",
   "Yet the boom is not only about health. A marathon has become a social event. Friends train together, cities close their streets, and strangers cheer from the pavement. For many participants, finishing a race is less about speed than about the wish to achieve a personal goal. The medal at the finish line is proof that steady, constant effort, not talent, made it happen. Many runners say it is the crowd's warm support, rather than the clock, that carries them through the hardest last few kilometres.",
   "Still, experts warn that enthusiasm must be matched with care. Training should increase gradually, and the body needs time to recover between long runs. Runners who ignore the early signs of injury often pay for it later. In the end, the marathon teaches a simple lesson that fits almost every part of life: lasting results come from measured, regular effort rather than one sudden burst. A slow and steady beginning, in other words, is the surest route to a strong finish."
  ],
  "zh": "本文从“马拉松不再是精英的专属”说起：随着收入提高、健康成为个人目标，跑步因装备少、易融入日常而迅速普及。规律运动能控制体重、强健心脏、降低多种疾病风险，还能带来清醒与平静。马拉松更演变为社交事件：朋友结伴训练、城市封路、路人加油，完成比赛与其说关乎速度，不如说是在实现个人目标。但专家提醒，热情须配以科学：训练要循序渐进，长跑之间注意恢复，忽视伤病信号往往要付出代价。结论是：持久的成果来自持续而适度的努力，而非一次爆发。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "The change did not happen by chance.",
    "cn": "这一变化并非偶然。",
    "why": "by chance 是固定搭配，意为“偶然、碰巧”，与“机会”无关；not ... by chance 常用来强调某事有其必然原因。"
   },
   {
    "en": "Finishing a race is less about speed than about the wish to achieve a personal goal.",
    "cn": "完成一场比赛，与其说关乎速度，不如说关乎实现个人目标的愿望。",
    "why": "less about A than about B 是“与其说A，不如说B”的比较句式，写作中用来纠正或深化对某事的理解。"
   },
   {
    "en": "Lasting results come from measured, regular effort rather than one sudden burst.",
    "cn": "持久的成果来自适度而规律的努力，而不是一时的爆发。",
    "why": "rather than 表示“而不是”，连接两个并列成分；measured 在此为“有分寸的、适度的”，不是“测量过的”。"
   }
  ],
